message: "If you use THE Q-MODEL (TQM), please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "THE Q-MODEL — From Q to Cosmology"
abstract: >-
  THE Q-MODEL (TQM) is a theory of structure and content that compresses observable
  physics to four primitives (the individuation principle Q, Random Actualization, the
  scale triad, and a single nonlinearity parameter M^2). It holds that the form of every
  structure is derivable from these primitives while the content is realized by contingent
  draw. The dynamical layer is the graph Laplacian L_Q; the derivation program yields U(1),
  spatial dimension 3+1, the multiplicity lower bound, the log-normal abundance law, and
  phase-gradient gravity whose leading order is the Einstein equations.
